Generic single-database configuration.

---

TransferIQ-specific notes
==========================

The schema is authored in database/schema.sql (loaded automatically by
Postgres on first container start via docker-entrypoint-initdb.d) and
mirrored in backend/app/models.py's SQLAlchemy ORM classes. Alembic was
adopted after both already existed and matched (as of 2026-09-12), so the
first migration (`baseline`) is a deliberate no-op -- it does not create
any tables. A fresh database still needs schema.sql; Alembic is stamped
onto it afterward with `alembic stamp head`, not run with `upgrade head`.

Workflow for a real future schema change:
    1. Edit backend/app/models.py (the two must never drift apart).
    2. Also update database/schema.sql to match, by hand.
    3. Run: alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
    4. READ the generated file before running anything. Autogenerate
       compares the live DB against models.py's ORM classes only -- if a
       table exists in schema.sql/the DB but has no ORM class (as was
       true for player_comparisons, watchlist_players, and
       player_comparison_players when Alembic was adopted), autogenerate
       will propose DROPPING it. Never run a migration you have not read.
    5. Run: alembic upgrade head

Known gap (as of the baseline migration): player_comparisons,
watchlist_players, and player_comparison_players exist in schema.sql and
the live database but have no ORM class in models.py yet. These are the
blueprint's optional, non-core auth/watchlist tables. Left as-is rather
than guessing whether to add classes or drop the tables.
